le between $u$ and $v$ is ${82}^{∘}$ and $n$ is the unit vector that points in the direction of $u\\times v.$ Find $u\\times v$ in terms of $n.$ \n\nType $n$ to represent the vector $n$ and round your final answer to **two decimal places** where appropriate.\n\n$u\\times v≈$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "We use the formula for the cross product and obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u\\times v & =|u|\\cdot |v|\\cdot \\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta \\cdot n \\\\  & =4\\cdot 5\\cdot \\operatorname{sin}⁡{82}^{∘}\\cdot n \\\\  & =20\\cdot (0.990\\,26…)\\cdot n \\\\  & =(19.805\\,2…)\\cdot n \\\\  & ≈19.81n.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-279282/field-1"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "09aeb7f5-31e0-5b2d-9e2a-8eace54a6665"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-279282"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]}]
